  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nHigh pressure centered over the Central Rockies will continue to\nbring very warm temperatures with widespread 90 degree \ntemperatures through the weekend and isolated triple digits on \nSunday. This upper ridging is expected to be the dominant force \nover the western U.S., extending into eastern Montana, through \nthe forecast cycle. \n\nWeak embedded shortwaves coupled with deep monsoonal moisture \nwill also be present as well bringing high PWATs and daily chances\nfor showers and thunderstorms. That said, the predictability of \nspecific timing and placement for convective behavior will be \ndifficult at larger time scales. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nBrought in stronger influence from HRRR for PoPs today to better\nmatch neighbors. Otherwise, followed NBM.",
